  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and the third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${p,q}$ with ${p,q}$ and ${2,4,6},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\times A\\times B={ & (p,p,2),(p,p,4),(p,p,6),(p,q,2),(p,q,4),(p,q,6), \\\\  & (q,p,2),(q,p,4),(q,p,6),(q,q,2),(q,q,4),(q,q,6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|A\\times A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(p,q,2)$ and $(q,q,6)$ are in $A\\times A\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
